<title>USA: Stimsonite says Robert Stutz named CEO.</title>
<headline>Stimsonite says Robert Stutz named CEO.</headline>
<dateline>NILES, Ill. 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stimsonite Corp said its board of directors elected Robert Stutz, 44, to fill the position of president and chief executive effective March 22.</p>
<p>Stutz was previously vice president of the automotive controls division of Cherry Electrical Products, a division of Cherry Corp, Stimsonite said.  </p>
<p>Stutz replaces Jay Taylor, who became a consultant to the company.</p>
<p>Stimsonite makes raised reflective pavement markers and optical film for use in the construction of highway signs.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
